# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# biometric-two-person — AI Act Art. 14(5): a SEPARATE, OPTIONAL add-on
# obligation for biometric-identification deployments, outside the core L0-L6
# ladder. It is not a grade-independent floor: nothing here declares a `grade`
# at all, so it composes with whatever rung governs the rest of the
# deployment (attach it alongside any Lx gate by granting the same actor over
# a `biometric-id-decision` kind) rather than replacing that rung's own
# obligation. Quorum with a conjunction target requires two DISTINCT parties
# (spec §6: the quorum distinctness predicate over provenance), which is this
# language's expression of "verified or confirmed by at least two natural
# persons... individually".
actor agent
human verifier1 role biometric-verifier
human verifier2 role biometric-verifier
gate  biometric-id risk critical grant agent
reserve biometric-id-decision by verifier1 and verifier2
cord  agent        -> biometric-id
cord  biometric-id -> master
